{{~##
   One constant set.

   The file is the module, so there is no `pub mod` wrapper here any more and no `use super::*`
   standing in for it - lib.rs declares `pub mod <set>;` and the public path a consumer writes
   is unchanged.

   The set's own comment arrives as the file head's `module_doc`, because a `///` needs an item
   to attach to and this file's contents are the item.
##~}}
{{ include 'rust-file-head.sbn' ~}}
{{~ for constant in set.constants ~}}
{{~ for line in constant.comment ~}}
/// {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
pub const {{ constant.name }}: {{ constant.type }} = {{ constant.value }};
{{~ end ~}}
